{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V48ZNMrL812zc1oGmdk7Vo","type":"tool_result","content":"127:## 3. Media Manager UI — Inline `SponsorsView`\n128-\n129-**File**: `show-controller/src/pages/MediaManagerPage.jsx`\n130-\n131-### Destructure from hook (lines 22-32)\n132-Add: `sponsors`, `saveSponsor`, `deleteSponsor`, `reorderSponsors`, `getTeamSponsors`, `getTeamSponsorCount`\n133-\n134-### Team card header (lines 344-394)\n135-Add sponsor count badge alongside existing status indicators: `\"3 Spons\"` (amber) or `\"No Spons\"` (zinc).\n136-\n137-### Expanded card (lines 398-404)\n138-Wrap `RosterView` + new `SponsorsView` in a fragment:\n139-\n140-```jsx\n141-{expandedTeam === team.key && (\n142-  <>\n143-    <RosterView ... />\n144-    <SponsorsView teamKey={team.key} ... />\n145-  </>\n146-)}\n147-```\n148-\n149-### SponsorsView component (new, after RosterView definition at line 648)\n150-\n151-**Props**: `{ teamKey, getTeamSponsors, saveSponsor, deleteSponsor, reorderSponsors }`\n152-\n153-**Layout**:\n154-```\n155-[Section header: \"Sponsors (N)\" with amber SparklesIcon]\n156-[Sponsor list - if any:]\n157-  Row: [48x48 logo thumbnail] [Name] [Tier badge] [Truncated URL] [Up] [Down] [Delete]\n158-  Row: ...\n159-[Add sponsor form - always visible:]\n160-  [Name input] [Logo URL input + 48x48 preview] [Tier dropdown] [Add button]\n161-[Empty state: \"No sponsors for this team\"]\n162-```\n163-\n164-**Behavior**:\n165-- **Add**: Enter name + logo URL + tier (dropdown: presenting/official/supporting, default \"official\"). On submit: auto-slugify name → `sponsorKey`, auto-set `order` to current count, call `saveSponsor(teamKey, sponsorKey, {...})`. Clear form on success.\n166-- **Duplicate key guard**: Before saving, check if `sponsorKey` already exists in `getTeamSponsors(teamKey)`. If it does, show an inline error: `\"A sponsor named '{name}' already exists for this team\"` and do NOT call `saveSponsor`. This prevents silent overwrites.\n167-- **Logo URL preview**: When URL is pasted, show a 48x48 inline thumbnail. Use `<img onError>` to show red broken-image warning. Do NOT block save on broken image.\n168-- **Reorder**: Up/Down arrow buttons call `reorderSponsors(teamKey, newOrderedKeys)` with the full recomputed key array (swap the two adjacent items in the sorted list, extract all keys in new order).\n169-- **Delete**: Trash icon, no confirmation (consistent with existing patterns). Calls `deleteSponsor(teamKey, sponsorKey)`.\n170-\n171----\n172-\n173-## 4. Overlay: sponsors-thanks.html\n174-\n175-**File**: `overlays/sponsors-thanks.html`\n176-\n177-**Follow existing overlay conventions** (see `overlays/event-frame.html`, `overlays/hosts.html`):\n178-- Viewport: `<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=1920, height=1080\">`\n179-- Font: Google Fonts Inter\n180-- Reset: `* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }`\n181-- Body: `width: 1920px; height: 1080px; overflow: hidden;`\n182-- URL params via: `const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);`\n183-\n184-**Header bar** (match overlay pattern):\n185-- Gray header bar (`#BFBFBF` background)\n186-- Title: \"THANK YOU TO OUR SPONSORS\" (left side)\n187-- Team logo (80x80, `object-fit: contain`) — far right\n188-- `background: transparent` for the body\n189-\n190-**URL params**:\n191-- `?logo={teamLogoUrl}` — team logo for the header bar\n192-- `?sponsors={encodedJSON}` — JSON array of `[{name, url}]` objects\n193-\n194-**Rendering**: Parse `sponsors` param, render logos in a CSS grid. Auto-sizing: 1-2 sponsors = single row; 3-4 = 2x2; 5-8 = 2 rows. Each sponsor: logo (200x200, `object-fit: contain`) + name below (24px).\n195-\n196-**Error handling**:\n197-\n198-| Condition | Behavior |\n199-|-----------|----------|\n200-| Missing/empty `?logo=` | Hide header logo element (`display:none`) |\n201-| Missing/empty `?sponsors=` | Show centered \"No sponsors configured\" |\n202-| Invalid JSON in `?sponsors=` | `try/catch` around `JSON.parse`; show \"No sponsors configured\" |\n203-| Empty array `[]` | Show \"No sponsors configured\" |\n204-| Broken sponsor logo URL | `img.onerror`: hide broken img, show fallback div with sponsor name in styled box |\n205-| Long sponsor name | `text-overflow: ellipsis; max-width: 200px; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden;` |\n206-\n207-> **Why URL params instead of Firebase**: All 16 existing overlay files use URL params exclusively — none use Firebase. This keeps overlays stateless, cacheable, and resilient to Firebase outages. The URL Builder serializes sponsor data from the React app (which already has the Firebase subscription) into the URL.\n208-\n209----\n210-\n211-## 5. Overlay: sponsors-cycle.html\n212-\n213-**File**: `overlays/sponsors-cycle.html`\n214-\n215-Same gray header bar as sponsors-thanks (`#BFBFBF`, title: \"OUR SPONSORS\", team logo on right).\n216-\n217-**Below the header**: One sponsor logo at a time, centered, large (~600px max, `object-fit: contain`). Sponsor name below logo (36px Inter bold). Crossfade transition (CSS opacity, 0.5s). 3-second hold. Continuous loop via `setInterval`.\n218-\n219-**URL params**: Same as sponsors-thanks.\n220-\n221-**Error handling**:\n222-\n223-| Condition | Behavior |\n224-|-----------|----------|\n225-| Missing/empty/invalid `?sponsors=` | Header + centered \"No sponsors\" message; no cycling |\n226-| Empty array `[]` | Same as missing |\n227-| 1 sponsor | Static display — no `setInterval`, no transitions |\n228-| Broken logo during cycle | `img.onerror` → call `advanceToNext()` immediately (skip broken sponsor) |\n229-| ALL logos broken | Track `brokenCount`; if equals `sponsors.length`, switch to text-only mode (show just names) |\n230-\n231-**Note on live updates**: URL-param-based overlays are static once loaded. If sponsors change mid-broadcast, the producer must regenerate and reload the URL in OBS. This matches every other overlay in the system.\n232-\n233----\n234-\n235-## 6.