{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LGksDKJjtUzSwv6L7917r5","type":"tool_result","content":"   250→\n   251→**Create new file:**\n   252→- 1920x1080 viewport, fully transparent body\n   253→- No header bar\n   254→- Container: `position: fixed; bottom: 40px; right: 40px; width: 200px; height: 80px;`\n   255→- Semi-transparent dark pill: `rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px;`\n   256→- 10s hold, 0.8s fade, continuous loop\n   257→- URL params: `?sponsors={encodedJSON}` only (no `?logo=`)\n   258→- Missing/empty → fully transparent page; 1 sponsor → static; all broken → hide container\n   259→\n   260→**Status:** COMPLETE\n   261→\n   262→---\n   263→\n   264→### T11: Build — Local Verification\n   265→\n   266→**Dependencies:** T1-T10\n   267→**Plan Reference:** [PLAN Section 9](./PLAN-Sponsor-System-2026-02-13.md#9-task-order)\n   268→\n   269→**Steps:**\n   270→1. `cd show-controller && npm run build`\n   271→2. Verify no errors, no warnings about missing imports\n   272→3. Check `dist/` output exists\n   273→\n   274→**Status:** COMPLETE\n   275→\n   276→---\n   277→\n   278→### T12: Deploy — Production\n   279→\n   280→**Dependencies:** T11\n   281→**Plan Reference:** [PLAN Deployment](./PLAN-Sponsor-System-2026-02-13.md#deployment)\n   282→\n   283→**Steps:**\n   284→1. Deploy React SPA (tarball → upload → extract)\n   285→2. Deploy 3 overlay files (rebuild overlays tarball → upload → extract)\n   286→3. Verify overlay URLs serve correct content:\n   287→   - `https://commentarygraphic.com/overlays/sponsors-thanks.html`\n   288→   - `https://commentarygraphic.com/overlays/sponsors-cycle.html`\n   289→   - `https://commentarygraphic.com/overlays/sponsors-bug.html`\n   290→4. Verify main site has no console errors\n   291→5. Verify URL Generator shows Sponsors sidebar section\n   292→\n   293→**Status:** COMPLETE\n   294→\n   295→---\n   296→\n   297→---\n   298→\n   299→### T13: Overlay — Smart Content Detection for White Backgrounds\n   300→\n   301→**File:** `overlays/sponsors-cycle.html`\n   302→**Dependencies:** None\n   303→**Plan Reference:** [PLAN Section 10](#10-smart-content-detection)\n   304→\n   305→**Problem:** `getContentBounds()` (line 196) only detects transparent pixels (`alpha > 20`) as content. JPEG images and PNGs with white/opaque backgrounds have alpha=255 for ALL pixels, so the entire image (including asymmetric whitespace) is treated as content. The canvas is centered by flexbox, but the visual content within it is off-center if the source image has uneven padding.\n   306→\n   307→**Changes:**\n   308→1. Enhance `getContentBounds()` to also detect near-white/near-background pixels as \"background\" — not just transparent ones\n   309→2. Add a two-pass detection strategy:\n   310→   - **Pass 1 (existing):** Scan for non-transparent pixels (alpha threshold). If the detected content is significantly smaller than the full image, use it (logo has transparency).\n   311→   - **Pass 2 (new):** If Pass 1 returns the full image (opaque image detected), scan for non-white/non-near-white pixels using a luminance or RGB threshold. Treat pixels where R>240, G>240, B>240 as background.\n   312→3. The threshold should be configurable but default to RGB > 240 for \"near-white\" detection\n   313→4. Keep the existing crop override system — manual crop always wins over auto-detection\n   314→\n   315→**Test cases:**\n   316→- Transparent PNG: Should trim to content bounds (existing behavior, unchanged)\n   317→- JPEG with white background: Should now trim white borders and center the actual logo content\n   318→- JPEG with colored background: Should fall back to full image (no trimming)\n   319→- Logo with light gray background (#E5E5E5): Should NOT trim since background matches page background\n   320→\n   321→**Status:** NOT STARTED\n   322→\n   323→---\n   324→\n   325→### T14: Data Model — Add Adjustment Fields to Sponsor CRUD\n   326→\n   327→**File:** `show-controller/src/hooks/useTeamsDatabase.js`\n   328→**Dependencies:** None (extends existing T1 work)\n   329→\n   330→**Changes:**\n   331→\n   332→1. **`saveSponsor()` (line 260):** Add optional adjustment fields to the Firebase write. These fields should only be written when they have non-default values (to keep Firebase clean):\n   333→   ```js\n   334→   await set(ref(db, `teamsDatabase/sponsors/${teamKey}/${sponsorKey}`), {\n   335→     name: sponsorData.name,\n   336→     url: sponsorData.url,\n   337→     tier: sponsorData.tier || 'official',\n   338→     order: sponsorData.order ?? 0,\n   339→     // Adjustment fields (only write if non-default)\n   340→     ...(sponsorData.scale != null && sponsorData.scale !== 100 ? { scale: sponsorData.scale } : {}),\n   341→     ...(sponsorData.offsetX ? { offsetX: sponsorData.offsetX } : {}),\n   342→     ...(sponsorData.offsetY ? { offsetY: sponsorData.offsetY } : {}),\n   343→     ...(sponsorData.cropX != null ? { cropX: sponsorData.cropX } : {}),\n   344→     ...(sponsorData.cropY != null ? { cropY: sponsorData.cropY } : {}),\n   345→     ...(sponsorData.cropW != null ? { cropW: sponsorData.cropW } : {}),\n   346→     ...(sponsorData.cropH != null ? { cropH: sponsorData.cropH } : {}),\n   347→     updatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n   348→   });\n   349→   ```\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ea1db2c-89c7-412f-b1f0-dadd8edabc6c","uuid":"46101e9a-8364-4df3-95ce-9c03ce40f6bd","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/juliacosmiano/code/gymnastics-graphics/docs/PRD-Sponsors/PLAN-Sponsor-System-Implementation.md","content":"\n**Create new file:**\n- 1920x1080 viewport, fully transparent body\n- No header bar\n- Container: `position: fixed; bottom: 40px; right: 40px; width: 200px; height: 80px;`\n- Semi-transparent dark pill: `rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px;`\n- 10s hold, 0.8s fade, continuous loop\n- URL params: `?sponsors={encodedJSON}` only (no `?logo=`)\n- Missing/empty → fully transparent page; 1 sponsor → static; all broken → hide container\n\n**Status:** COMPLETE\n\n---\n\n### T11: Build — Local Verification\n\n**Dependencies:** T1-T10\n**Plan Reference:** [PLAN Section 9](./PLAN-Sponsor-System-2026-02-13.md#9-task-order)\n\n**Steps:**\n1. `cd show-controller && npm run build`\n2. Verify no errors, no warnings about missing imports\n3. Check `dist/` output exists\n\n**Status:** COMPLETE\n\n---\n\n### T12: Deploy — Production\n\n**Dependencies:** T11\n**Plan Reference:** [PLAN Deployment](./PLAN-Sponsor-System-2026-02-13.md#deployment)\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Deploy React SPA (tarball → upload → extract)\n2. Deploy 3 overlay files (rebuild overlays tarball → upload → extract)\n3. Verify overlay URLs serve correct content:\n   - `https://commentarygraphic.com/overlays/sponsors-thanks.html`\n   - `https://commentarygraphic.com/overlays/sponsors-cycle.html`\n   - `https://commentarygraphic.com/overlays/sponsors-bug.html`\n4. Verify main site has no console errors\n5. Verify URL Generator shows Sponsors sidebar section\n\n**Status:** COMPLETE\n\n---\n\n---\n\n### T13: Overlay — Smart Content Detection for White Backgrounds\n\n**File:** `overlays/sponsors-cycle.html`\n**Dependencies:** None\n**Plan Reference:** [PLAN Section 10](#10-smart-content-detection)\n\n**Problem:** `getContentBounds()` (line 196) only detects transparent pixels (`alpha > 20`) as content. JPEG images and PNGs with white/opaque backgrounds have alpha=255 for ALL pixels, so the entire image (including asymmetric whitespace) is treated as content. The canvas is centered by flexbox, but the visual content within it is off-center if the source image has uneven padding.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. Enhance `getContentBounds()` to also detect near-white/near-background pixels as \"background\" — not just transparent ones\n2. Add a two-pass detection strategy:\n   - **Pass 1 (existing):** Scan for non-transparent pixels (alpha threshold). If the detected content is significantly smaller than the full image, use it (logo has transparency).\n   - **Pass 2 (new):** If Pass 1 returns the full image (opaque image detected), scan for non-white/non-near-white pixels using a luminance or RGB threshold. Treat pixels where R>240, G>240, B>240 as background.\n3. The threshold should be configurable but default to RGB > 240 for \"near-white\" detection\n4. Keep the existing crop override system — manual crop always wins over auto-detection\n\n**Test cases:**\n- Transparent PNG: Should trim to content bounds (existing behavior, unchanged)\n- JPEG with white background: Should now trim white borders and center the actual logo content\n- JPEG with colored background: Should fall back to full image (no trimming)\n- Logo with light gray background (#E5E5E5): Should NOT trim since background matches page background\n\n**Status:** NOT STARTED\n\n---\n\n### T14: Data Model — Add Adjustment Fields to Sponsor CRUD\n\n**File:** `show-controller/src/hooks/useTeamsDatabase.js`\n**Dependencies:** None (extends existing T1 work)\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`saveSponsor()` (line 260):** Add optional adjustment fields to the Firebase write. These fields should only be written when they have non-default values (to keep Firebase clean):\n   ```js\n   await set(ref(db, `teamsDatabase/sponsors/${teamKey}/${sponsorKey}`), {\n     name: sponsorData.name,\n     url: sponsorData.url,\n     tier: sponsorData.tier || 'official',\n     order: sponsorData.order ?? 0,\n     // Adjustment fields (only write if non-default)\n     ...(sponsorData.scale != null && sponsorData.scale !== 100 ? { scale: sponsorData.scale } : {}),\n     ...(sponsorData.offsetX ? { offsetX: sponsorData.offsetX } : {}),\n     ...(sponsorData.offsetY ? { offsetY: sponsorData.offsetY } : {}),\n     ...(sponsorData.cropX != null ? { cropX: sponsorData.cropX } : {}),\n     ...(sponsorData.cropY != null ? { cropY: sponsorData.cropY } : {}),\n     ...(sponsorData.cropW != null ? { cropW: sponsorData.cropW } : {}),\n     ...(sponsorData.cropH != null ? { cropH: sponsorData.cropH } : {}),\n     updatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n   });\n   ```","numLines":100,"startLine":250,"totalLines":538}}}
